<title>POLAND: ZEW EXTENDS TUMBLE ON FLOOD DAMAGE.</title>
<headline>ZEW EXTENDS TUMBLE ON FLOOD DAMAGE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish electrode maker ZEW SA fell the daily maximum 10 percent for the second day running, dropping a total of 23.2 percent to 23.5 zlotys since resuming trade on Monday after a month-long flood suspension.</p>
<p>Last month ZEW, based in the badly hit town of Raciborz, said it had incurred losses exceeding 50 million zlotys due to the flooding but would receive full insurance compensation.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
